<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28414" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕgărĭcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεγαρικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the city of
				Megara, Megaric</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 7, 4, § 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Megaricus sinus,</span>”
				<i>a part of the Saronic Gulf, near Megara</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 4,
					12, 19, § 57</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">signa,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of marble from Megara</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 1, 8, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 9, 2</span></i>.— <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕgărĭci</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., sc. philosophi,
				<i>the followers of Euclid</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 42, 129</span></i>.</div>
